    rdf:value """Friday April 29. 1898. Frullino Florence 
A quiet day. I called on the Buttles, and then met Etta McArthur and her nurse at the train and brought them here. She is very ill and cannot walk a step.
---
Story written by a little boy of 7.
Virtue has its own reward
A poor young man fell in love with the daughter of a rich lady who kept a candy shop. The poor young man could not marry the rich candy lady’s daughter because he had not enough money to buy any furniture. A wicked man offered to give the young man $25 if he would become a drunkard. The young man wanted to marry very much, so he could marry the rich candy lady’s daughter, but when he got to the saloon he turned to the wicked man and said, ‘I will not become a drunkard. Get thee """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 30 ;
